        <mxCell id="note_more" value="&lt;b&gt;Reading the gateway arrow, and what is not drawn&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The gateway's one arrow is ten allows: it reaches :8080 in every fenced namespace (identity for the id route and remoteJWKS; inventory's pods only), and also :9090 in review, notification and shipping, whose allow names no port. All ten service namespaces reach identity :8080 for the JWKS, since their pkg/authmw verifier is fail-closed; monitoring reaches identity :9000 / :8080 (the data-tier diagram); payment admits its own namespace on :8080 for mockpay. Allows into inventory and product's :9090 select only the service pods (pod-scoped)." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="850" width="910" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note_missing" value="&lt;b&gt;The arrow that does not exist&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nothing may call checkout on :9090: it is a gRPC client of the mesh, never a server to it. Only the gateway reaches checkout, on :8080." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="942" width="910" height="40" as="geometry" />
